➡Java's introduction of Stream Gatherers is a powerful enhancement in the Stream API.

➡Stream gatherers allow us to transform streams in more flexible ways than was previously possible using standard collectors.

➡Think of gatherers as the missing piece between map() and collect(): they give us fine-grained control over how data is grouped, reordered, or buffered as it flows through a stream, providing a more declarative and composable solution to stream reshaping.

