⚠️ 𝗔 𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗱 𝗼𝗳 𝗖𝗮𝘂𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻

As powerful as Stream Gatherers are, they’re not a drop-in replacement for every stream use case. A few things to keep in mind:

🔹 They are stateful – which means they may not parallelize well. Many gatherers (like scan() or windowFixed()) work sequentially and could break or produce incorrect results if used in parallel streams.

🔹 Not all problems need a gatherer. For simple transformations (map(), filter(), collect()), using gatherers is like using a chainsaw to cut a toothpick—unnecessary and possibly dangerous to maintain.

🔹 Debugging can be tricky. Gatherers, like complex collectors, can sometimes obscure logic if overused. Clear, well-named custom methods can help, but imperative code may still be the clearer path for some workflows.

